18#,#18 Major (General)#,#General Mathematics#,#Bachelor of Science in Mathematics (General Mathematics Option)

The mathematics major leads to the Bachelor of Science in Mathematics. In addition to the General Institute Requirements, the requirements consist of Differential Equations (18.03), plus eight additional 12-unit subjects in Course 18 of essentially different content, including at least six advanced subjects (first decimal digit one or higher). One of these eight subjects must be Linear Algebra.

required_subjects
restricted_electives
communication

%% Core requirement: Differential Equations (plus linear algebra choice)
required_subjects, "Required Subjects" := 18.03, (18.06/18.700/18.701)

%% Eight 12-unit electives, 6+ must be advanced (first decimal >= 1)
